; The Raspberry Pi 5's devices, the one table of them: each line a base, a
; length, a name for tests, or - for none, and what it is. tools/boards.l0
; writes pi5-aarch64-devices.ll from it, and spec boards/pi5.md lists the
; same; pi5-aarch64.ll says why each is a region. tools/test.sh --virt
; fails when the written file is not what this table gives.
0x107D001000 0x1000 - the debug UART, a PL011
0x107C003000 0x1000 - the 1 MHz system timer
0x107C013880 0x40 - the VideoCore mailbox
0x1F00000000 0x414000 - RP1's BAR1, BAR2, BAR0
0x107C580000 0x1A000 - the HVS
0x1000005200 0x80 - iommu4, the HVS's IOMMU
0x1000005B00 0x80 - iommuc, the IOMMUs' cache
0x1000120000 0x9310 - the PCIe controller of RP1
0x107C700000 0x4800 - HDMI0's blocks, one run
0x107C720000 0x100 - the HD block
0x107C410000 0x100 - pixel valve 0
0x107D508200 0x58 - DDC0
0x1000010600 0x100 - dma40's channel 6
0x1000FFF000 0x600 - sdio1, SDHCI and cfg
0x107C502000 0x30 - disp_intr
